cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tomoz, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Tomoz: deterministic learned lossless compression of medical image volumes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "González-Vázquez"
    given-names: "Joaquin J."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3352-8844"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZeroXShot/tomoz"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
abstract: >-
  Tomoz is a lossless codec for medical image volumes (CT, MR, PET and
  projection images) based on TZ1, a small integer neural context model with
  adaptive entropy coding whose output is bit-identical across CPU kernels,
  thread counts and WebAssembly.
keywords:
  - lossless compression
  - medical imaging
  - learned compression
  - DICOM
  - deterministic inference
